1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,266
I'm Peppa Pig. Oink.

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:07,466
-This is my little brother George.
-Oink, oink!

3
00:00:08,233 --> 00:00:10,299
This is Mommy Pig. Oink!

4
00:00:10,366 --> 00:00:12,333
-And this is Daddy Pig.
-Oink!

5
00:00:12,399 --> 00:00:13,799
[laughing]

6
00:00:14,166 --> 00:00:15,233
Peppa Pig.

7
00:00:16,566 --> 00:00:19,500
Edmond Elephant's Birthday.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,466
[car horn plays "Taps"]

9
00:00:22,099 --> 00:00:25,700
[narrator] Mr. Zebra the Postman
is delivering a letter to Peppa's house.

10
00:00:27,066 --> 00:00:30,200
Oh, look.
Someone's got a party invitation.

11
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,166
It must be for me.

12
00:00:32,233 --> 00:00:36,333
It says, "To George Pig,
from Edmond Elephant.

13
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:38,033
Please come to my party."

14
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:41,033
Doesn't it say "George and Peppa"?

15
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,199
-No. Just George.
-Hmmph.

16
00:00:43,266 --> 00:00:47,400
I didn't want to go
to a silly baby party anyway.

17
00:00:47,466 --> 00:00:49,199
[telephone ringing]

18
00:00:50,199 --> 00:00:51,099
Hello?

19
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:54,733
Oh, it's for you, Peppa.
It's Emily Elephant.

20
00:00:55,133 --> 00:00:56,666
-Hello.
-Hello, Peppa.

21
00:00:56,733 --> 00:00:57,666
[rock music playing]

22
00:00:57,733 --> 00:01:00,433
Do you want to come to Edmond's party
as my friend?

23
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:02,300
Oh, yes, please.

24
00:01:02,366 --> 00:01:05,666
My mommy wants us to help
with the little ones.

25
00:01:05,733 --> 00:01:08,433
Help? Yes, I can help.

26
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:11,366
Danny and Suzy are helpers, too.

27
00:01:11,433 --> 00:01:13,000
Oh, goody.

28
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:14,733
[children laughing]

29
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:18,366
[narrator] Everyone is here
for Edmond Elephant's party.

30
00:01:18,433 --> 00:01:19,399
[giggling]

31
00:01:19,466 --> 00:01:21,133
Oh! The helpers are here.

32
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,033
[in unison] Hello, Mrs. Elephant.

33
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:25,233
Let's get this party started.

34
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:28,333
Who wants to play Musical Statues?

35
00:01:28,399 --> 00:01:29,466
[in unison] Yay!

36
00:01:29,533 --> 00:01:31,366
This is what you do.

37
00:01:31,533 --> 00:01:33,500
Dance when the music is playing...

38
00:01:33,566 --> 00:01:34,566
[polka music playing]

39
00:01:34,633 --> 00:01:37,366
...and when it stops,
freeze like a statue.

40
00:01:37,433 --> 00:01:38,433
[music stops]

41
00:01:39,366 --> 00:01:41,600
Ready, steady, go.

42
00:01:41,666 --> 00:01:43,500
[music starts]

43
00:01:43,566 --> 00:01:45,800
Just dance already.

44
00:01:46,033 --> 00:01:47,566
[laughing]

45
00:01:47,633 --> 00:01:49,000
[music stops]

46
00:01:50,533 --> 00:01:52,666
This one is still blinking.

47
00:01:52,733 --> 00:01:53,800
You're out.

48
00:01:54,033 --> 00:01:55,166
[sobbing]

49
00:01:55,233 --> 00:01:57,766
[music starts, then stops]

50
00:01:58,399 --> 00:02:01,433
You're moving, George. You're out.

51
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:03,333
[sobbing, then squeals]

52
00:02:03,399 --> 00:02:06,000
Richard and Edmond are out.

53
00:02:06,699 --> 00:02:09,133
So, Zaza is the winner.

54
00:02:09,199 --> 00:02:10,100
Hooray!

55
00:02:10,166 --> 00:02:11,366
You've got a medal.

56
00:02:11,433 --> 00:02:14,500
It's made of real plastic gold.

57
00:02:14,566 --> 00:02:16,400
-[giggles]
-[sobbing]

58
00:02:17,666 --> 00:02:21,200
-Mommy, Musical Statues is over.
-[sobbing continues]

59
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:22,366
Lovely.

60
00:02:23,533 --> 00:02:26,100
Now it's time for Pass the Parcel.

61
00:02:26,166 --> 00:02:27,066
[all] Yay!

62
00:02:27,133 --> 00:02:31,233
When the music plays,
pass the parcel round.

63
00:02:31,299 --> 00:02:35,500
When the music stops, take some paper off.

64
00:02:35,566 --> 00:02:38,133
Ready, steady, go.

65
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,400
[music starts]x

66
00:02:41,266 --> 00:02:44,433
George. Pass the parcel.

67
00:02:45,799 --> 00:02:46,799
[music stops]

68
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:50,100
[narrator] Edmond has got a medal.
-[laughs]

69
00:02:50,166 --> 00:02:51,766
[music starts, then stops]

70
00:02:54,166 --> 00:02:56,066
Hurry up, Richard.

71
00:02:56,133 --> 00:02:59,133
Just take the paper off.

72
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:02,766
[narrator] Richard has got a medal.
-[giggles]

73
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,066
[music starts, then stops]

74
00:03:05,666 --> 00:03:07,400
[narrator] George has got a medal.

75
00:03:07,466 --> 00:03:08,633
Oink, oink! [giggles]

76
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:11,533
[music starts, then both grunting]

77
00:03:13,299 --> 00:03:14,633
Pass the parcel.

78
00:03:16,033 --> 00:03:19,266
[narrator]
Oh, dear. George isn't passing the parcel.

79
00:03:19,333 --> 00:03:20,266
[music stops]

80
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,399
-Oink, oink! [giggles]
-[wails]

81
00:03:24,299 --> 00:03:27,799
No, George. That's Zaza's medal.

82
00:03:28,033 --> 00:03:29,166
[wails]

83
00:03:29,233 --> 00:03:30,333
[music starts]

84
00:03:35,166 --> 00:03:36,066
[music stops]

85
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:38,299
[laughs]

86
00:03:38,366 --> 00:03:39,766
It's a giant teddy.

87
00:03:40,399 --> 00:03:41,733
[narrator] Edmond has won.

88
00:03:41,799 --> 00:03:42,799
[wailing]

89
00:03:45,333 --> 00:03:48,100
Mommy, Pass the Parcel is finished.

90
00:03:48,666 --> 00:03:50,799
Lovely. Now it's time for food.

91
00:03:51,033 --> 00:03:52,200
[in unison] Hooray!

92
00:03:52,266 --> 00:03:53,366
[giggling]

93
00:03:53,433 --> 00:03:56,533
[narrator]
Oh, the helpers have taken all the seats.

94
00:03:57,166 --> 00:04:02,266
This is Edmond's party, remember?
The helpers can eat after the little ones.

95
00:04:02,333 --> 00:04:03,600
[in unison] Oh, yes.

96
00:04:03,666 --> 00:04:05,366
We're the helpers.

97
00:04:07,799 --> 00:04:09,033
Juice, please.

98
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:11,466
-Juice, please.
-Juice, please.

99
00:04:11,533 --> 00:04:14,100
-Jelly, please.
-Jelly. Jelly.

100
00:04:14,166 --> 00:04:15,700
More, please.

101
00:04:17,633 --> 00:04:19,766
Happy birthday, Edmond.

102
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,333
[in unison] Happy birthday, Edmond.

103
00:04:25,433 --> 00:04:27,533
[narrator] It is the end of the party.

104
00:04:27,599 --> 00:04:29,500
Thank you to the helpers.

105
00:04:29,566 --> 00:04:32,166
You all worked really hard.

106
00:04:32,333 --> 00:04:36,366
Yes. It's not easy
looking after little children.

107
00:04:36,433 --> 00:04:39,333
[sighs] I need to lie down.

108
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,300
I need a holiday.

109
00:04:48,233 --> 00:04:51,300
[Peppa]
The Biggest Muddy Puddle in the World.

110
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:54,300
[narrator]
It is bedtime for Peppa and George.

111
00:04:55,033 --> 00:04:57,366
Oink. There's so much rain.

112
00:04:57,433 --> 00:05:00,599
That means there will be puddles
to jump in tomorrow.

113
00:05:00,666 --> 00:05:04,566
-Oh, goody.
-You can never have too much rain.

114
00:05:05,433 --> 00:05:06,566
[thunder rumbles]

115
00:05:09,733 --> 00:05:11,066
[rooster crows]

116
00:05:12,099 --> 00:05:13,200
[narrator] It is morning.

117
00:05:13,266 --> 00:05:14,333
Hooray!

118
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:16,700
Muddy puddles.

119
00:05:16,766 --> 00:05:18,400
-[giggling]
-[quacks]

120
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:23,066
Oh, hello, Mrs. Duck.
What are you doing here?

121
00:05:23,566 --> 00:05:25,000
-Oink.
-[all] Wow.

122
00:05:25,066 --> 00:05:27,700
[narrator] The rain has made a flood.

123
00:05:28,033 --> 00:05:31,766
Our house is a desert island.

124
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:36,700
Muddy puddles, here I come. Wee!

125
00:05:38,333 --> 00:05:40,266
-Oh?
-[quacks]

126
00:05:40,333 --> 00:05:42,500
Who put all this water here?

127
00:05:44,666 --> 00:05:46,566
How will we get our food?

128
00:05:46,633 --> 00:05:50,500
Daddy will have to swim to the shops.

129
00:05:50,566 --> 00:05:52,366
-Uh...
-[bell rings]

130
00:05:52,433 --> 00:05:55,666
[narrator]
Grandpa Pig has arrived on his boat.

131
00:05:55,733 --> 00:06:00,200
Ahoy, there. Wonderful boating weather.

132
00:06:00,266 --> 00:06:01,266
Um...

133
00:06:01,333 --> 00:06:02,333
Yes.

134
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:05,766
We're sailing to the shops.
Do you need anything?

135
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:10,233
Yes, please. Can you get us
some tomatoes and spaghetti?

136
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:12,233
Tomatoes and spaghetti.

137
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:15,200
[announcer] Polly Parrot copies everything
that is said.

138
00:06:15,266 --> 00:06:17,233
Polly can be our shopping list.

139
00:06:17,433 --> 00:06:19,766
-Who's a clever parrot?
-[squawks]

140
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,666
Who's a clever parrot?

141
00:06:21,733 --> 00:06:24,266
-Can we come, too, please?
-Oink!

142
00:06:24,333 --> 00:06:25,400
Hop aboard.

143
00:06:33,033 --> 00:06:36,799
Look. There's Suzy Sheep's house.

144
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:39,266
We're going to the shops.

145
00:06:39,633 --> 00:06:41,799
Do you need anything?

146
00:06:42,033 --> 00:06:45,533
Mommy, do we need anything
from the shops?

147
00:06:45,599 --> 00:06:48,033
[mommy sheep]
Yes. We need food for dinner.

148
00:06:48,099 --> 00:06:50,066
Chocolate, please.

149
00:06:50,133 --> 00:06:51,599
[squawks] Chocolate.

150
00:06:56,066 --> 00:06:58,299
-Hello, Danny.
-[barks]

151
00:06:58,366 --> 00:06:59,700
Hello, Peppa.

152
00:06:59,766 --> 00:07:02,200
I'm helping my granddad.

153
00:07:02,266 --> 00:07:06,599
-We're rescuing people.
-Great weather for it.

154
00:07:06,666 --> 00:07:10,266
-Do you need anything from the shops?
-Uh...

155
00:07:10,366 --> 00:07:12,200
Maybe a newspaper.

156
00:07:12,266 --> 00:07:13,733
And a comic.

157
00:07:13,799 --> 00:07:15,766
Newspaper. Comic.

158
00:07:19,033 --> 00:07:23,200
Grandpa, what's that stick thing
in the water?

159
00:07:23,433 --> 00:07:27,466
Ah! Submarine. Actions stations.

160
00:07:27,533 --> 00:07:29,566
[bell rings, then alarm sounds]

161
00:07:30,299 --> 00:07:33,166
Ahoy, there, me hearties.

162
00:07:33,233 --> 00:07:36,299
[narrator]
It's Grampy Rabbit in his submarine.

163
00:07:36,366 --> 00:07:41,533
Lovely day to go sailing
with just the sea and the sky.

164
00:07:41,599 --> 00:07:45,166
-The stories I could tell--
-Do you need any shopping?

165
00:07:45,233 --> 00:07:49,133
-Oh, yes. Uh, cheese, please.
-Cheese.

166
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:53,666
[narrator] Grandpa Pig's boat has arrived
at the supermarket.

167
00:07:55,166 --> 00:07:58,066
Hello. It's very quiet today.

168
00:07:58,133 --> 00:08:01,733
-You're my first customers.
-Oink. Maybe it's because of the flood.

169
00:08:01,799 --> 00:08:03,466
Silly, isn't it?

170
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:07,433
A little bit of rain,
and everyone stays at home.

171
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:09,066
What can I get you?

172
00:08:09,133 --> 00:08:11,299
Polly has a list.

173
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:13,133
Who's a clever parrot?

174
00:08:13,466 --> 00:08:15,299
Who's a clever parrot?

175
00:08:15,366 --> 00:08:19,066
[narrator]
Oh, dear. Polly has forgotten the list.

176
00:08:19,133 --> 00:08:23,400
Luckily, I remember what everyone wants.

177
00:08:24,733 --> 00:08:26,033
Cheese.

178
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:29,766
Thank you, Peppa. You're a good 'un.

179
00:08:30,666 --> 00:08:32,666
Newspaper and comic.

180
00:08:32,733 --> 00:08:34,633
-Thanks, Peppa.
-Thanks, Peppa.

181
00:08:35,366 --> 00:08:40,166
It was lucky Peppa was going to the shops,
or we'd have nothing for dinner.

182
00:08:40,233 --> 00:08:41,699
Here's your chocolates.

183
00:08:42,299 --> 00:08:44,766
Now we can have our dinner, Mommy.

184
00:08:47,533 --> 00:08:50,133
[narrator]
Peppa and George have arrived back home.

185
00:08:50,566 --> 00:08:52,133
It is their bedtime.

186
00:08:55,633 --> 00:08:57,233
It is morning.

187
00:08:59,566 --> 00:09:00,466
Oh!

188
00:09:00,533 --> 00:09:04,566
[narrator] The water has gone
but left a big muddy puddle.

189
00:09:05,266 --> 00:09:06,766
Muddy puddles.

190
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:07,733
[giggling]

191
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:13,633
This is the biggest muddy puddle
in the world, ever.

192
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,333
[Peppa] Santa's Grotto.

193
00:09:21,666 --> 00:09:23,333
[narrator] It is Christmas Eve.

194
00:09:24,133 --> 00:09:27,233
Hands up who wants to go
and see Father Christmas.

195
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:28,766
-Me. Me. Me.
-Me. Me. Me.

196
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,266
Are we going to the North Pole?

197
00:09:31,333 --> 00:09:33,133
Not quite that far, Peppa.

198
00:09:33,199 --> 00:09:36,766
But Father Christmas lives
at the North Pole.

199
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:41,166
Lucky for us, he's got a grotto
at the Christmas fair.

200
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:46,000
[narrator] Peppa and George have come
to visit Santa's Grotto.

201
00:09:46,066 --> 00:09:48,433
-Hello, everyone.
-[in unison] Hello.

202
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,266
All aboard the Elf Train.

203
00:09:50,733 --> 00:09:53,033
This way to Santa's Grotto.

204
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:54,199
[train horn toots]

205
00:09:54,266 --> 00:09:58,233
Suzy, what are you asking
Father Christmas For?

206
00:09:58,300 --> 00:10:01,533
I don't know. What are you asking for?

207
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:08,033
I would like a doll that walks and talks
and closes its eyes when it goes to sleep.

208
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:09,633
I'll ask for that, too.

209
00:10:09,699 --> 00:10:14,166
How does Father Christmas remember
what toys everybody wants?

210
00:10:14,233 --> 00:10:15,433
He makes a list.

211
00:10:16,066 --> 00:10:21,100
His sleigh must be very fast
to go around the whole world in one night.

212
00:10:21,166 --> 00:10:23,300
It's a super sleigh.

213
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:26,433
Father Christmas is really old.

214
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:28,433
He's hundreds of years old.

215
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:31,066
Even older than my Daddy.

216
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:37,066
-Santa's Grotto.
-[children] Ooh!

217
00:10:37,133 --> 00:10:41,266
Ho-ho-ho! Hello, everyone.

218
00:10:41,333 --> 00:10:43,400
[in unison] Hello, Father Christmas.

219
00:10:43,466 --> 00:10:46,400
-Have you all been good?
-Yes.

220
00:10:46,466 --> 00:10:51,066
-Have you all kept your bedrooms tidy?
-Yes.

221
00:10:51,133 --> 00:10:52,033
Have you?

222
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:54,066
Ha-ha-ho! Of course.

223
00:10:54,133 --> 00:10:57,733
Now, come and tell me
what you'd like for Christmas.

224
00:10:57,800 --> 00:11:00,400
[barks] Can I have a football, please?

225
00:11:00,466 --> 00:11:02,600
-A xylophone.
-Tiddly winks.

226
00:11:02,666 --> 00:11:06,433
-A magic set, please.
-Racing car.

227
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:07,600
[imitates racing car engine]

228
00:11:07,666 --> 00:11:10,566
Bouncy ball. Boing! Boing!

229
00:11:10,633 --> 00:11:12,600
A train, please.

230
00:11:12,666 --> 00:11:14,633
A toy train.

231
00:11:14,699 --> 00:11:18,733
Not a toy train. A real train.

232
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:23,199
One I can drive, with real passengers.

233
00:11:23,266 --> 00:11:26,266
Ho, ho! I'll see what I can do.

234
00:11:26,633 --> 00:11:28,300
Is that everyone?

235
00:11:28,366 --> 00:11:30,566
We haven't seen you yet.

236
00:11:30,633 --> 00:11:34,300
I am sorry. What is your name?

237
00:11:34,366 --> 00:11:37,666
Oink. I'm Peppa Pig. We've met before.

238
00:11:37,733 --> 00:11:41,699
Ah, yes. Nice to see you again, Peppa.

239
00:11:41,766 --> 00:11:44,066
What would you like for Christmas?

240
00:11:44,133 --> 00:11:47,333
I would like a doll that walks and talks

241
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:51,533
and closes its eyes when it goes to sleep,
please.

242
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:52,500
Um...

243
00:11:52,566 --> 00:11:56,266
-The same for me, please.
-Very good.

244
00:11:56,333 --> 00:11:59,100
You do know where I live, don't you?

245
00:11:59,166 --> 00:12:00,566
Oh, yes.

246
00:12:00,633 --> 00:12:02,066
How old are you?

247
00:12:02,133 --> 00:12:05,366
Ho, ho! I'm hundreds of years old.

248
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:06,666
I told you.

249
00:12:07,266 --> 00:12:09,266
Goodbye, Father Christmas.

250
00:12:09,333 --> 00:12:13,466
-Don't forget to leave me a mince pie--
-And a drink.

251
00:12:13,533 --> 00:12:14,600
We know.

252
00:12:14,666 --> 00:12:17,199
And a carrot for the reindeer.

253
00:12:17,266 --> 00:12:19,066
Ho-ho-ho!

254
00:12:20,366 --> 00:12:24,300
[narrator] Peppa and her family
are driving back from the Christmas Fair.

255
00:12:24,366 --> 00:12:27,533
Daddy, why have we got our bags
in the car?

256
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:31,266
We're spending Christmas
at Granny and Grandpa's house.

257
00:12:31,333 --> 00:12:34,533
But Father Christmas won't know
where we are.

258
00:12:34,599 --> 00:12:38,566
Don't worry, Peppa.
Father Christmas knows everything.

259
00:12:39,199 --> 00:12:40,099
[horn honks]

260
00:12:40,166 --> 00:12:43,066
Granny Pig. It's nearly Christmas.

261
00:12:43,133 --> 00:12:46,699
Yes, and I've got a very important job
for you.

262
00:12:47,333 --> 00:12:50,500
Stir the Christmas pudding
and make a wish.

263
00:12:51,300 --> 00:12:54,199
[narrator]
Peppa and George are making a wish.

264
00:12:54,266 --> 00:12:55,666
Racing car.

265
00:12:55,733 --> 00:12:57,666
Oh, don't tell me what it is.

266
00:13:00,133 --> 00:13:04,266
Here's the mince pie and a drink
for Father Christmas.

267
00:13:04,333 --> 00:13:07,033
And a carrot for the reindeer.

268
00:13:07,766 --> 00:13:08,633
[doorbell chimes]

269
00:13:08,699 --> 00:13:11,366
Who can that be at this time of night?

270
00:13:11,433 --> 00:13:14,199
We're not buying anything.

271
00:13:14,666 --> 00:13:18,333
♪ Merry, joyful greetings
Festive, happy cheer ♪

272
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:19,400
Carol singers.

273
00:13:19,466 --> 00:13:22,800
♪ Snow is falling gently
Christmas time is here ♪

274
00:13:23,033 --> 00:13:24,366
Oh, Merry Christmas.

275
00:13:24,433 --> 00:13:27,000
[narrator]
It is bedtime for Peppa and George.

276
00:13:27,066 --> 00:13:30,266
This used to be my bedroom
when I was a little piggy.

277
00:13:30,333 --> 00:13:34,433
Father Christmas knows
where Granny and Grandpa live, doesn't he?

278
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:38,000
Oh, yes. He's been here many times before.

279
00:13:38,066 --> 00:13:40,533
Good night, Peppa. Good night, George.

280
00:13:40,599 --> 00:13:41,533
[snoring]

281
00:13:41,599 --> 00:13:44,000
[narrator]
Peppa and George have fallen asleep.

282
00:13:44,166 --> 00:13:47,300
When they wake up,
it will be Christmas day.

283
00:13:49,366 --> 00:13:51,633
[Peppa] Santa's Visit.

284
00:13:51,699 --> 00:13:54,133
[narrator]
It is very early on Christmas morning.

285
00:13:54,199 --> 00:13:58,266
Peppa and her family are staying
at Granny and Grandpa Pig's house.

286
00:13:58,599 --> 00:14:00,433
George, wake up.

287
00:14:01,033 --> 00:14:02,766
-Oink, oink!
-Santa's been.

288
00:14:03,766 --> 00:14:05,199
Bubble mix.

289
00:14:07,033 --> 00:14:08,199
Comics.

290
00:14:08,266 --> 00:14:10,133
And tangerines.

291
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:15,066
Mommy. Daddy. It's Christmas.

292
00:14:15,133 --> 00:14:18,133
-Eh? What?
-It's too early, Peppa.

293
00:14:18,199 --> 00:14:21,766
Go and say Happy Christmas
to Granny and Grandpa.

294
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,433
[snoring]

295
00:14:23,533 --> 00:14:25,199
Granny. Grandpa.

296
00:14:25,266 --> 00:14:26,133
[screams]

297
00:14:26,199 --> 00:14:29,266
UDon't panic. All hands on deck. [snorts]

298
00:14:29,333 --> 00:14:31,099
It's Christmas.

299
00:14:31,166 --> 00:14:33,400
It's three o'clock in the morning.

300
00:14:33,466 --> 00:14:35,400
But Santa's been.

301
00:14:35,466 --> 00:14:37,766
Can we see if he's still here?

302
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:40,766
No, Santa's not here.

303
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:45,233
Look, the carrot, drink and mince pie
have gone.

304
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:47,400
He's only left crumbs.

305
00:14:47,466 --> 00:14:51,166
Yes. Santa likes a good mince pie.

306
00:14:51,233 --> 00:14:54,300
And there are big presents under the tree.

307
00:14:54,566 --> 00:14:58,800
I asked Santa for a doll.
Can we open them now?

308
00:14:59,033 --> 00:15:02,633
We will open the big presents
after Christmas lunch.

309
00:15:02,699 --> 00:15:04,266
Oh, goody.

310
00:15:05,599 --> 00:15:08,599
[narrator] Peppa and her family
are having Christmas lunch.

311
00:15:08,666 --> 00:15:10,266
Let's pull the crackers.

312
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:15,300
There are paper hats inside.

313
00:15:15,366 --> 00:15:17,333
And party trumpets.

314
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,233
And jokes.

315
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:23,533
-What wobbles in the sky?
-I don't know.

316
00:15:23,599 --> 00:15:25,000
A jelly copter.

317
00:15:27,466 --> 00:15:32,766
-Mmm. This Christmas pudding is delicious.
-Peppa and George helped me make it.

318
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,500
-We did the stirring.
-Did you make a wish, Peppa?

319
00:15:36,566 --> 00:15:39,433
-Yes, I wished for--
-Don't tell us.

320
00:15:40,633 --> 00:15:42,333
Let's open the presents.

321
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:43,599
Yippee!

322
00:15:43,666 --> 00:15:45,733
This one is for George.

323
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:47,000
Oink, oink!

324
00:15:48,599 --> 00:15:50,666
[narrator] It is a racing car set.

325
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:53,300
[Grandpa] This looks a bit complicated.

326
00:15:53,699 --> 00:15:55,233
Let me see.

327
00:15:55,300 --> 00:16:00,300
This goes here, and that goes there,
and this goes there.

328
00:16:00,366 --> 00:16:02,300
Oink! Let's race.

329
00:16:02,366 --> 00:16:04,699
Ready, steady, go.

330
00:16:04,766 --> 00:16:05,733
[imitating car engine]

331
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:09,633
[narrator] Daddy and Grandpa
are enjoying playing racing cars.

332
00:16:09,699 --> 00:16:12,133
-Isn't that George's present?
-[laughs]

333
00:16:12,199 --> 00:16:15,366
I think George is quite happy
playing with the box.

334
00:16:15,433 --> 00:16:17,233
[imitates car engine]

335
00:16:17,699 --> 00:16:19,766
This is your present, Daddy Pig.

336
00:16:21,033 --> 00:16:24,366
-Ah! Socks.
-And I've got socks.

337
00:16:24,733 --> 00:16:26,666
-Socks.
-Socks.

338
00:16:26,733 --> 00:16:28,233
-Socks.
-[all laughing]

339
00:16:28,333 --> 00:16:32,000
So, the last present must be for--

340
00:16:32,066 --> 00:16:35,033
Me. I asked Santa
for a doll that walks and talks

341
00:16:35,099 --> 00:16:37,633
and closes its eyes when it goes to sleep.

342
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:39,199
Oh!

343
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:40,466
Birdseed?

344
00:16:41,166 --> 00:16:42,266
Birdseed.

345
00:16:42,333 --> 00:16:44,466
That present is for Polly Parrot.

346
00:16:44,533 --> 00:16:47,000
But it was the last one.

347
00:16:47,066 --> 00:16:49,566
Santa has forgotten me.

348
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:52,333
[ringing]

349
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:54,033
-Hello?
-[bleats]

350
00:16:54,099 --> 00:16:56,666
Can I talk to Peppa, please?

351
00:16:56,733 --> 00:16:58,766
Peppa. It's Suzy Sheep.

352
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,400
Hello, Suzy.

353
00:17:00,466 --> 00:17:03,233
-Did you get your doll?
-No.

354
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:04,366
I got mine.

355
00:17:04,433 --> 00:17:08,566
It cries and laughs
and closes its eyes and everything.

356
00:17:08,633 --> 00:17:11,233
Santa's given you my doll.

357
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:15,333
No. The label says, "For Suzy Sheep."

358
00:17:15,399 --> 00:17:18,433
Oink. Then Santa has forgotten me.

359
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:21,733
Ho-ho-ho!

360
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:24,099
[narrator] Santa is on his way home.

361
00:17:24,166 --> 00:17:28,466
That's the last of this year's toys
delivered.

362
00:17:28,533 --> 00:17:32,133
Oh! What's this at the bottom of my sack?

363
00:17:33,133 --> 00:17:35,200
Santa can't have forgotten you.

364
00:17:35,266 --> 00:17:38,233
I have been a good piggy, haven't I?

365
00:17:40,333 --> 00:17:42,566
Ho-ho-ho!

366
00:17:42,633 --> 00:17:43,700
Santa.

367
00:17:43,766 --> 00:17:47,533
-Uh... Hello.
-He came down our chimney.

368
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:49,766
Of course he did, Granny.

369
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:53,100
Here's your present, Peppa.

370
00:17:53,166 --> 00:17:54,766
Sorry it's a bit late.

371
00:17:56,233 --> 00:17:58,166
[giggles] My doll.

372
00:17:58,233 --> 00:18:00,233
Thank you, Santa.

373
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:05,700
-Would you like some Christmas pudding?
-George and I stirred it and made wishes.

374
00:18:05,766 --> 00:18:07,566
Mmm! Yummy.

375
00:18:07,633 --> 00:18:12,666
And I wished that Santa would visit us
on Christmas Day.

376
00:18:12,733 --> 00:18:14,066
And you did.

377
00:18:14,133 --> 00:18:16,066
Ho-ho-ho!

